<!--
  Daily market close newsletter.

  Install:
    cp daily_email/com.leon.dailyclose.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.leon.dailyclose.plist 2>/dev/null
    launchctl load   ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.leon.dailyclose.plist

  Run once immediately:  launchctl start com.leon.dailyclose
  Uninstall:             launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.leon.dailyclose.plist

  WHY FIVE TIMES A DAY, NOT ONE:
  The NYSE calendar can report a session closed hours before Yahoo publishes its
  bars -- on 2026-09-22 the 16:45 data was still a day stale at 21:00. A single
  attempt therefore either sends the PREVIOUS session's numbers or nothing at
  all. Each attempt re-checks; daily_close.py refuses to send stale data and
  records every session it emails, so exactly one newsletter goes out per
  session no matter how many attempts run. A skipped attempt costs ~5 seconds.

  The 08:00 slot is the catch-up: it covers a Mac asleep through every evening
  attempt, sending the previous session late rather than losing it.

  That slot only started working in Sep 2026. daily_close.py used to refuse to
  send unless the last completed session was TODAY (ET), so at 08:00 -- when the
  last completed session is always the previous day -- every catch-up run bailed.
  A session the machine slept through was therefore lost for good; 2026-09-25 was
  lost exactly this way. The gate is gone: any completed session missing from
  sent_sessions.txt is now sent whenever a run next manages to fire.

  Start/stop this job from the Streamlit sidebar (Daily Newsletter panel) rather
  than by hand -- it bootstraps AND enables, so a Stop survives the next login.

  This machine is on Eastern time, so local == market time.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.leon.dailyclose</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <!-- caffeinate -i: once a run starts, keep the Mac from idle-sleeping until
             it ends. Without it a run that launchd starts in a dark-wake window
             is put back to sleep mid-network-call (2026-09-30: hung 7 h). -->
        <string>/usr/bin/caffeinate</string>
        <string>-i</string>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/uv</string>
        <string>run</string>
        <string>--directory</string>
        <string>/Users/leonyip/Code/stock_analysis_tool</string>
        <string>python</string>
        <string>daily_email/daily_close.py</string>
        <string>--email</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/leonyip/Code/stock_analysis_tool</string>

    <!-- launchd inherits almost no environment; PATH must be explicit. -->
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <!-- ET (the Mac's local zone). The 21-23h slots exist so a Mac that slept
         through the evening sends within the hour of being woken; launchd also
         fires one missed slot on wake. Extra slots are free: the duplicate
         check exits before any HTTP. Keep in sync with newsletter_control.SLOTS. -->
